AArch64 SpinlockSwpl3
(* Spinlock released by a release-only swap: `spinlock_swp3.kl` with the
   release `STLR WZR,[X0]` replaced by `SWPL WZR,W2,[X0]` (writes 0, the old
   value goes to W2). Test-and-test-and-set shape: SWPA to acquire, LDR spin
   while held, SWPL release. SWPL rather than SWPAL: the release needs only
   release ordering (on the claim-conditional environment `EnvGC` the
   acquire half would make the swap claim the slots of the message it
   reads, for nothing).
   Three threads each take the lock once and increment a shared counter.
   Property: counter = 3 in every final state. Expected: Always.
   Proved for all layouts and any number of threads: `swpl_counter_envG`
   (Promising/SLR/EnvG/SwplLockPublic.lean), the first lock with an RMW
   release (KNOWN_GAPS.md, RMWREL, "Lifted").
   The shared symbols are typed (`uint32_t lock`, `uint32_t counter`, the width of every access)
   so that the runner declares them as sized locations at the width of
   the code's accesses (A64DECLS): the runner's
   declarations then agree with the proofs' locations. The code block and
   the verdict are unchanged. Proved from the runner's exact configuration
   (declarations and initial memory included): `swpl_counter_envG_runner`, concrete
   `swpl_counter_envG_runner_concrete3` (Promising/SLR/EnvG/A64SwplRunner.lean).
   Proved no fault at the runner's declarations (each access resolves as
   at `decls = {}`): `swpl_counter_envG_runner_noFault`, concrete
   `swpl_counter_envG_runner_noFault_concrete` (Promising/SLR/EnvG/A64NoFaultDLocks.lean).
   Proved program-level fault freedom at the runner's declarations (no
   reachable configuration has a faulting step, any architecture, promises
   included): `swpl_counter_envG_runner_faultFree`, concrete
   `swpl_counter_envG_runner_faultFree_concreteN 3` (Promising/SLR/EnvG/A64FaultFreeFixed.lean).
   Proved both at once (safety and fault freedom, at the union of their
   hypotheses): `swpl_counter_envG_runner_safe_faultFree`, concrete
   `swpl_counter_envG_runner_safe_faultFree_concreteN 3` (Promising/SLR/EnvG/RunnerSafeFFA64.lean).
   Proved (LIVESPIN2): promise-free deadlock-freedom on a valid layout,
   `Live.SpinSwpFam.spin_swpl_live_pf [ValidLayout (layout swplWorker)] : SwplSpinLivePF fuel`,
   concrete `spin_swpl_live_pf_concrete`; per-thread liveness of these one-shot
   workers `spin_swpl_live_oneShot_pf` (Promising/LiveSpinSwpFam.lean). With
   promises (`SwplSpinLive`) open (KNOWN_GAPS.md, "Liveness: spinlocks (LIVESPIN)").
   Proved (LIVESPINSEM2): with promises and semantic certification,
   `Live.SpinSemSwpLive.spin_swpl_live_sem [ValidLayout (layout swplWorker)] : SwplSpinLiveSem fuel`
   for every fuel, concrete `spin_swpl_live_sem_concrete`, and the one-shot
   `spin_swpl_live_oneShot_sem` (Promising/LiveSpinSemSwpLive.lean). `SwplSpinLive`
   (over `succs`) stays open (KNOWN_GAPS.md). *)
# flags: -sym
# expect: Always
{
uint32_t lock=0; uint32_t counter=0;
0:X0=lock; 0:X1=counter;
1:X0=lock; 1:X1=counter;
2:X0=lock; 2:X1=counter;
}
threads { P0: worker done; P1: worker done; P2: worker done; }
code {
worker:
  MOV W3,#1
try:
  SWPA W3,W2,[X0]
  CBZ W2,cs
spin:
  LDR W2,[X0]
  CBNZ W2,spin
  B try
cs:
  LDR W5,[X1]
  ADD W5,W5,#1
  STR W5,[X1]
  SWPL WZR,W2,[X0]
  B done
done:
}
forall [counter]=3
